Third-party components
----------------------

The packages contain third-party components that are licensed under their own terms, which take
precedence over the terms above for the components they cover. A running Emiro server lists every
one of them, with its license text, under "Licenses" in the account menu.

Some of these components - the FFmpeg libraries among them - are licensed under the GNU Lesser
General Public License. For those components, nothing in the terms above restricts the rights that
license grants. In particular, you may modify the software for your own use and reverse engineer
it to the extent needed to debug such modifications, and you may replace the LGPL libraries the
software loads with modified versions of them. The complete corresponding source code of each LGPL
component, including any changes made to it, is listed on the same page and can be downloaded from
it.
